      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Pangasius nasutus (Bleeker, 1863). Family: Pangasiidae. Maximum size: 90 cm SL. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</p><p>Etymology: the name Pangasius comes from a local (Bengali) name of the fish (pungas).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1243",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Greater Sunda Island rivers in Sumatra and Borneo, and Peninsular Malaysia. Type locality: Barito River, Bandjarmasin, southern Kalimantan, Borneo, Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1243",
      "html": "<p>Needs a large amount of open space for swimming room and some plants to help reduce the nervous nature of the fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1243",
      "html": "<p>Females are fuller-bodied.</p>"
    },
    {
